Rihanna used some Fenty Beauty math to reveal she has &#8220;at least&#8221; 170 songs in the stash ready to go at the moment.

&#8220;If there are 10 products in a vault, then I have at least 17 vaults,&#8221; she said. Doing some quick math to solve Rihanna&#8217;s equation, 17 times 10 equals the 170 songs she&#8217;s cryptically referring to.

Rihanna&#8217;s partner, A$AP Rocky, who shares three kids with the beauty mogul, divulged that Rih was back in the studio and actively recording during an August interview with Jason Lee.

“Yo, she in the studio right now,&#8221; he begrudingly disclosed. &#8220;Yeah, I said it. Sorry, babe. Like, bro, she working. She cooking, no funny sh&#8211;. Damn, I’mma get in trouble for this.&#8221;

There hasn’t been much noise when it comes to Rihanna’s plans for new music. Rih&#8217;s last release came in 2025 and saw her contribute to the  Smurfs Movie  soundtrack with “Friend of Mine.&#8221;

ANTI arrived in 2016 and spent two weeks atop the&nbsp; Billboard 200.&nbsp; Rihanna returned to the stage in July as part of&nbsp; Jay-Z’s &nbsp; Extra Innings show &nbsp;at Yankee Stadium and performed “Run This Town” and “Bitch Better Have My Money.”
